  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 478,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "A cardiovascular drug: WHERE does it act? That predicts its use and what rules it OUT",
   "lines": [
    "where each fits in a regimen: see the HYPERTENSION TREATMENT, HEART FAILURE and ATRIAL FIBRILLATION charts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_r",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 120,
   "w": 440,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "Block the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system (RAAS)",
   "lines": [
    "all of them RAISE K+: watch it, most in renal insufficiency"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_h",
   "x": 525,
   "y": 120,
   "w": 666,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "Act on the HEART: rate and force",
   "lines": [
    "ACUTE HF with a fast rate: digoxin, or a LOW-dose beta blocker; NOT diltiazem (negative inotrope)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_v",
   "x": 1231,
   "y": 120,
   "w": 440,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "Dilate the VESSELS",
   "lines": [
    "headache, hypotension, reflex tachycardia"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ac_head_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 260,
   "w": 214,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "ac_h",
   "title": "ACE inhibitor (-pril) · ARB (-sartan)",
   "lines": [
    "angiotensin receptor blocker (ARB)"
   ]
  },
  {
